  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the circle containing the points $(1,3)$, $(1,-1)$, $(3,1)$. Hint: Sketch these points.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(x-1)^2+(y-1)^2=2^2$.",
      "worked": "The points $(1,3)$ and $(1,-1)$ are equally spaced above and below $y=1$, so the centre lies on $y=1$. Let the centre be $C(a,1)$. Equal distances to $(1,3)$ and $(3,1)$ give\n$$\\begin{align*}(1-a)^2+(3-1)^2&=(3-a)^2\\\\1-2a+a^2+4&=9-6a+a^2\\\\4a&=4\\\\a&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe centre is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $2$. Therefore,\n$$(x-1)^2+(y-1)^2=2^2.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
